<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ricote Valley</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Valle de Ricote</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ricote Valley is a stretch of the Segura river valley in the Region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murcia">Murcia</a>, south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, known for irrigated orchards laid out in the Islamic period. In 1228 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-hud">Ibn Hud</a> began his rising against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a> there. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moriscos">Morisco</a> population was among the last in Spain to be expelled, in 1613–1614, after the general expulsion of the Moriscos.</p></div>
